# --- Product repo mount points (split layout, FWADR-021) ----------------------
# This framework directory is the TRACKED PARENT: it holds CLAUDE.md, docs/,
# .claude/ and the planning corpus. Each product lives in its OWN git repo,
# cloned into one of the mount points below. $CODE_ROOT = <parent>/<mount>.
#
#   majorrepo/    primary product repo   (DEFAULT_CODE_SUBDIR in .env)
#   minorrepo/    secondary service/tool (W-item `target-repo:` per FWADR-020)
#   mkt_website/  marketing site         (separate deploy cadence from product)
#
# The parent must never track their contents — a nested repo would otherwise be
# recorded as a stray gitlink, and every product commit would dirty the parent.
#
# These are ignored OUTRIGHT rather than preserved with a committed .gitkeep,
# deliberately: `git clone <url> majorrepo` REFUSES a non-empty destination
# ("destination path already exists and is not an empty directory" — verified
# 2026-07-29), so a tracked placeholder would block the exact workflow the
# mount points exist for. Consequence: a fresh clone of this parent will NOT
# contain them. Recreate with:
#
#   mkdir -p majorrepo minorrepo mkt_website
#
# Rename freely per project — update DEFAULT_CODE_SUBDIR in .env to match.
majorrepo/
minorrepo/
mkt_website/
